DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     zzeeddiitt is the text editor of the COHERENT GUI.  It must be
     run under the zzvviieeww desktop; started elsewhere it exits im-
     mediately.  It edits one plain-text file in a resizable win-
     dow with a scrollbar on the left edge and a status line
     showing the file name, a * when the buffer is modified, and
     the cursor position as _l_i_n_e, _c_o_l_u_m_n.

     With a _f_i_l_e argument zzeeddiitt loads that file; if it does not
     exist yet, editing starts in an empty buffer under that
     name.  With no argument the buffer starts empty and un-
     titled.  zzeeddiitt also accepts the standard window _o_p_t_i_o_n_s of
     GUI applications (-TT -II -SS -PP -HH); see zzvviieeww.

     The keyboard commands follow the MicroEMACS convention of
     control keys and prefix chords.  The C900 cursor keypad
     works as expected: the desktop translates the arrow keys and
     the keypad Home, End, PgUp, PgDn, Del and Enter keys into
     the corresponding control keys below.

     Cursor motion:

                ^BB          left one character (wraps to previous line)
                ^FF          right one character (wraps to next line)
                ^PP          up one line
                ^NN          down one line
                ^AA          to start of line
                ^EE          to end of line
                ^ZZ          up one page
                ^VV          down one page
                EESSCC <       to top of file
                EESSCC >       to end of file
                EESSCC ff       forward one word
                EESSCC bb       back one word
                ^LL          recentre the cursor line

     Editing:

                BBSS          delete left; at column 0, join with previous line
                DDEELL, ^DD     delete right; at end of line, join with next line
                ^KK          kill to end of line; repeated, appends and takes
                            the newline too
                ^WW          kill the selection
                ^YY          yank (insert the last killed text)
                ^OO          open a line below the cursor
                ^TT          transpose the characters around the cursor
                ^GG          abort; drop the selection

