     Printable characters and TAB insert at the cursor.  Tabs are
     stored literally and displayed at 8-column stops.  RETURN
     splits the line at the cursor.

     The mouse places the cursor with a left click, and a left
     drag selects text; on release the selection becomes the
     PRIMARY selection, which a middle click pastes in any GUI
     window (at the click point).  Cut and Copy instead use the
     clipboard, a separate store, so a clipboard paste and a mid-
     dle-click paste can carry different text.

     The window menu offers New, Open, Save, Cut, Copy, Paste and
     Help above the standard window entries.  Menu Save always
     shows the file-name dialog, prefilled with the current name;
     FF22 saves silently under the current name.  In dialogs, TAB
     cycles among text fields, RETURN fires the default button
     and ESC cancels.

